<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>LLM API access</title>
<style>
  body {
    background: #1a1a2e;
    color: #e6e6e6;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 2rem auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 2rem; color: #9d7bea; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; }
  td { padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #333; vertical-align: top; }
  td:first-child { color: #9d9d9d; white-space: nowrap; width: 1%; }
  code, pre {
    font-family: "SF Mono", Consolas, Menlo, monospace;
    background: #12121e;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  td code { padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem; }
  pre { padding: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; }
  a { color: #9d7bea; }
  .warn {
    background: #2e2410;
    border: 1px solid #5a4a1a;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    margin: 1.2rem 0;
  }
  .warn strong { color: #e0b84a; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>LLM API access</h1>
<p>Text below is selectable — drag to select just the part you need.</p>

<table>
  <tr><td>Endpoint</td><td><code>https://DOMAIN_PLACEHOLDER:8080/v1</code></td></tr>
  <!-- Replace MODEL_NAME_PLACEHOLDER below with whatever you set MODEL_FILE
       to in .env (without the .gguf extension is fine, it's just a label). -->
  <tr><td>Model</td><td><code>MODEL_NAME_PLACEHOLDER</code></td></tr>
  <tr><td>API key</td><td><code>sk-local</code> (any non-empty value — not checked)</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="warn">
  <strong>Before connecting a CLI tool or SDK (curl, a VSCode extension, etc.):</strong>
  unlike a browser, these don't let you click through an untrusted-certificate warning — they just
  fail outright with an error like <code>unable to verify the first certificate</code>. That means
  the machine running the tool needs your private certificate authority trusted at the OS level first.
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">
    <a href="https://DOMAIN_PLACEHOLDER/ca.crt">Download the CA certificate</a> (<code>ca.crt</code>), then:
  </p>
  <ul style="margin-top:0.4rem">
    <li><strong>Linux:</strong> <code>sudo cp ca.crt /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/local-llm-ca.crt && sudo update-ca-certificates</code></li>
    <li><strong>Windows:</strong> double-click <code>ca.crt</code> → Install Certificate → Local Machine → "Trusted Root Certification Authorities"</li>
    <li><strong>macOS:</strong> open in Keychain Access → System keychain → double-click it → set "Always Trust"</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">This is a one-time step per machine. Browsers don't need this — only non-browser tools.</p>
</div>

<h2>curl</h2>
<pre>curl https://DOMAIN_PLACEHOLDER:8080/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "MODEL_NAME_PLACEHOLDER",
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "hello"}]
  }'</pre>

<h2>VSCode / Continue</h2>
<p>Add as an OpenAI-compatible provider: set the base URL to the endpoint above, model name as above, any string as the API key.</p>

<h2>OpenCode</h2>
<p><code>~/.config/opencode/opencode.json</code> — add a provider with <code>baseURL</code> set to the endpoint above.</p>
<pre>{
  "provider": {
    "local-llama": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "options": { "baseURL": "https://DOMAIN_PLACEHOLDER:8080/v1" },
      "models": { "MODEL_NAME_PLACEHOLDER": { "name": "MODEL_NAME_PLACEHOLDER" } }
    }
  }
}</pre>

<p>Full details: <a href="https://DOMAIN_PLACEHOLDER:3000">OpenWebUI</a> for chat, or see the project's <code>docs/api.md</code>.</p>
</body>
</html>
